-----BEGIN PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----
Comment: This is a placeholder for the Tor Browser developers' signing
Comment: keyring. Replace it with the actual armored keys from
Comment: https://support.torproject.org/tbb/how-to-verify-signature/
Comment: ("Importing tor developers (signing) key") before relying on
Comment: GPG verification for shipped builds.
Comment:
Comment: How to populate this file:
Comment:   gpg --auto-key-locate nodefault,wkd --locate-keys \
Comment:       torbrowser@torproject.org
Comment:   gpg --output scripts/tor-signing-keys.asc --armor \
Comment:       --export torbrowser@torproject.org
Comment:
Comment: The fingerprint to confirm out-of-band:
Comment:   EF6E 286D DA85 EA2A 4BA7  DE68 4E2C 6E87 9329 8290
Comment:
Comment: fetch-tor-binaries.sh accepts an empty/placeholder keyring and
Comment: will WARN-but-continue. Replacing this file with the real keys
Comment: turns the warning into a hard fail on signature mismatch.
-----END PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----
